From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:24:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] windows.devices.display: Resolve only reported monitors and
 use base EDID facts.

Hold win32u's display_device_init mutex while resolving a monitor and
reading its facts, so a snapshot never straddles a display reconfiguration
that rebuilds the monitor device nodes. Resolve only monitors with an
enabled (linked) monitor interface, for both identifier forms, and include
InterfaceEnabled in the device selector.

Read the adapter LUID with the type win32u writes (UINT64), so the adapter
device ID resolves. Prefer the validated EDID product name to the generic
description written for every monitor node. Do not guess a usage kind for
virtual monitors.

Use base EDID 1.4 facts where no DisplayID declaration provides them: the
colour characteristics (all four points in the chromaticity domain or
none) and a preferred timing that EDID 1.4 declares native. A DisplayID
section with a reserved product primary use is left opaque.

Tests cover unlinked interfaces, connector validity (HD15 is zero),
virtual origin, base EDID facts, EDID 1.3 preferred timing, the reserved
use case, a short non-zero tail and adapter resolution on real topology.
---
